{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Brings.WignerTargetEquivariance","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Brings.WignerTargetEquivariance","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Brings.S5CharactersOnBringDeformations","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.Basic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.two_invariants_in_hh0_of_base","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.two_invariants_in_hh0_of_base","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/WignerTargetEquivariance.lean#L66-L70","doc":"The invariant part that does exist: `HH₀` of the base carries two invariants\n(`⟨χ_{HH₀}, 1⟩ = 240/120 = 2`), the rank and the point class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.no_invariant_in_hh2_of_base","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.no_invariant_in_hh2_of_base","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/WignerTargetEquivariance.lean#L59-L64","doc":"**The ledger entry:** `H¹(T_{Σ₄}) = [4,1] ⊕ [3,2]` has no `S₅`-invariant, so\n`HH²` of the base cannot receive the observable line equivariantly. Read off the\ncharacter table (`S5Char.hochschild_invariants_of_base`, fourth conjunct). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.equivariant_map_vanishes_of_no_invariants","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.equivariant_map_vanishes_of_no_invariants","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/WignerTargetEquivariance.lean#L50-L57","doc":"**No invariants in the target ⇒ every equivariant map from an invariant vector is\nzero.** The observable line is spanned by an invariant vector; if the target has no\nnon-zero invariants, its realisation there vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.equivariant_image_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.equivariant_image_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/WignerTargetEquivariance.lean#L42-L48","doc":"An additive `G`-equivariant map sends invariant vectors to invariant vectors. ","signatureChunk":0}]}